The ``open`` and ``short`` parameters of ``KeysightE4980ACorrection`` have been replaced by
methods of the same name. Both were command-only parameters, so calling them without an
argument, e.g. ``meter.correction.open()`` as in the example notebook, only returned the cached
value and did not execute the OPEN or SHORT correction. Calling them like this now sends the
command. Code that passed a value to them, e.g. ``meter.correction.open(None)``, must drop the
argument, and they are no longer part of the instrument's parameters or snapshot.
